D("rampant",{etymology:E("From Old French rampant, the present participle of ramper ‘climb, creep upward’; it first described an animal rearing on its hind legs and broadened to uncontrolled spread or growth.",null,"ramper","-ant","Etymonline, rampant (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rampant)."),contexts:[C("rampant.s1","公共衛生","With no vaccination campaign, measles became rampant across the district and overwhelmed the small clinics.","由於沒有接種疫苗的行動，麻疹在整個地區猖獗蔓延，讓小型診所不堪負荷。","Rampant means spreading quickly and becoming difficult to control.","Rampant describes measles; across gives the area of spread, and with introduces the cause.","The disease spreads widely and exceeds local control capacity.") ,C("rampant.s2","園藝","The ivy was rampant along the stone wall, sending new shoots over the gate and into the orchard.","常春藤沿著石牆蔓生，新枝越過大門伸進果園。","For a plant, rampant means growing thickly over a large area.","Rampant modifies ivy; sending introduces the visible result of its growth.","The vine's shoots spread beyond the wall into nearby space.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The ivy was rampant, yet it stayed inside one small pot and produced no spreading shoots.","The ivy was contained in one small pot and produced no spreading shoots.","Rampant describes vigorous spreading growth, which conflicts with a plant that remains confined.")],quiz:[Q("rampant.q1","rampant.s1","meaning","If fraud becomes rampant, it is ___.",["spreading widely and hard to control","limited to one corrected case","formally ranked by the court"],"spreading widely and hard to control","Rampant describes something spreading without effective control.","meaning"),Q("rampant.q2","rampant.s2","context","Which garden plant is rampant?",["A vine covers the fence and keeps growing into neighboring beds.","A seed remains sealed in a drawer.","A trimmed hedge stays within its boundary."],"A vine covers the fence and keeps growing into neighboring beds.","The vine is growing vigorously across a large area.","context"),Q("rampant.q3","rampant.s1","word-choice","Officials acted quickly to stop ____ price-fixing across the industry.",["rampant","rancid","ranked"],"rampant","The price-fixing is widespread and difficult to control.","word-choice"),Q("rampant.q4","rampant.s2","meaning","In heraldry, a “lion rampant” is shown ___.",["rearing upright on its hind legs","lying flat asleep","running on all four legs"],"rearing upright on its hind legs","The older heraldic sense depicts an animal rearing up.","meaning")]});
D("ranch",{etymology:E("From American Spanish rancho ‘small farm, group of farm huts’, earlier a place or group for eating together; its deeper route through Spanish ranchear and French ranger is commonly traced to Germanic rang, but details are uncertain.",null,"rancho",null,"Etymonline, ranch (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ranch)."),contexts:[C("ranch.s1","農業","The family runs a cattle ranch in Wyoming, where several hundred animals graze across the open range.","這個家族在懷俄明州經營牧牛場，數百頭牛在開闊牧地上吃草。","A ranch is a large farm in the Americas where livestock are raised.","Ranch is the object of runs; where introduces its location and animals grazing explain the operation.","It is a large livestock farm in the western United States.") ,C("ranch.s2","農業","The coastal ranch raises oysters rather than cattle, sending fresh shellfish to nearby restaurants.","這座沿海養殖場養的是牡蠣而非牛隻，並把鮮蚵送到附近餐館。","Ranch can also name a specialised farm that raises one kind of animal or crop.","Ranch is the subject; raises takes oysters as its object and rather than contrasts cattle.","The word refers to a specialist production farm, not only a cattle property.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The ranch consisted only of a downtown desk, with no land, animals, crops, or farming operation.","The ranch included grazing land and livestock managed as a working farm.","A ranch is a farm or livestock operation, not merely an unrelated office desk.")],quiz:[Q("ranch.q1","ranch.s1","meaning","A cattle ranch is primarily a ___.",["large livestock farm","city courthouse","printed proof sheet"],"large livestock farm","Ranches are large farms where cattle or other livestock are raised.","meaning"),Q("ranch.q2","ranch.s2","context","Which could be called a specialist ranch?",["A farm that raises oysters for restaurants","A shop that sells only notebooks","A mountain range with no farming"],"A farm that raises oysters for restaurants","The source entry allows a specialised farm raising one crop or animal.","context"),Q("ranch.q3","ranch.s1","word-choice","The family moved to a ____ to raise horses on open land.",["ranch","rancor","ranking"],"ranch","A ranch is a large livestock farm suited to raising horses.","word-choice"),Q("ranch.q4","ranch.s1","context","What work would most likely happen on a ranch?",["Managing grazing cattle","Proofreading a novel's typeset pages","Announcing a court verdict"],"Managing grazing cattle","Ranch work commonly involves raising and managing livestock.","context")]});
D("rancher",{etymology:E("From American Spanish ranchero ‘person living on or managing a rancho’, from rancho; English rancher names someone who owns or works on a ranch.",null,"rancho","-er","Etymonline, ranch (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ranch)."),contexts:[C("rancher.s1","農業","The rancher checked the water troughs before moving the cattle to a greener pasture.","牧場主先檢查飲水槽，才把牛群趕往草色更綠的牧地。","A rancher is a person who owns or works on a ranch.","Rancher is the subject; checked and moving describe the day's livestock work.","The person manages cattle and facilities on a working ranch.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The rancher managed the ranch's cattle but had no connection to the ranch or its work.","The rancher managed the ranch's cattle as part of the ranch's work.","A rancher is someone who owns or works on a ranch, so having no connection contradicts the role.")],quiz:[Q("rancher.q1","rancher.s1","meaning","A rancher most likely works with ___.",["livestock on a ranch","court transcripts in a courtroom","the proof of a theorem"],"livestock on a ranch","A rancher owns or works on a livestock ranch.","meaning"),Q("rancher.q2","rancher.s1","context","Who is the rancher in a news report?",["The person who manages cattle and pasture on the ranch","A tourist taking one photo of a horse","A printer checking a page proof"],"The person who manages cattle and pasture on the ranch","Managing the working ranch is the rancher's occupation.","context"),Q("rancher.q3","rancher.s1","word-formation","What does -er indicate in rancher?",["a person associated with or doing the work","a place where cattle graze","the past tense of ranch"],"a person associated with or doing the work","Here -er forms a person noun from ranch.","word-formation"),Q("rancher.q4","rancher.s1","word-choice","The ____ hired two hands to repair the cattle fence.",["rancher","rancid","randomly"],"rancher","The person who manages the ranch hires workers for its operation.","word-choice")]});
D("ranching",{etymology:E("Formed from ranch + the activity suffix -ing; ranch entered English from American Spanish rancho. Ranching names the business or practice of raising livestock on open ranch land.",null,"ranch","-ing","Etymonline, ranch (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ranch)."),contexts:[C("ranching.s1","農業","Ranching remains important in the dry plateau, where cattle graze over land too sparse for intensive crops.","在這片不適合密集耕作的乾燥高原上，牧場畜牧仍然很重要，牛隻在廣闊草地上吃草。","Ranching is the practice of raising livestock on a ranch.","Ranching is the subject; where explains the conditions that suit it.","The activity depends on extensive grazing land rather than small pens.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Ranching in the report meant keeping one pet rabbit in an apartment as a hobby.","Ranching in the report meant raising livestock across a working ranch.","Ranching refers to livestock production on ranch land, not keeping one household pet.")],quiz:[Q("ranching.q1","ranching.s1","meaning","Ranching is the business of ___.",["raising livestock on a ranch","selling printed proofs","ranking university applicants"],"raising livestock on a ranch","The noun names livestock raising as a ranch activity.","meaning"),Q("ranching.q2","ranching.s1","context","Which landscape most naturally supports ranching?",["A wide dry grassland where cattle can graze","A tiny indoor office with no animals","A city library reading room"],"A wide dry grassland where cattle can graze","Open grazing land is associated with ranching.","context"),Q("ranching.q3","ranching.s1","word-formation","In ranching, what does -ing help form?",["a noun naming an activity","a noun naming a person","a past-tense verb"],"a noun naming an activity","Ranching names the activity or occupation of raising livestock.","word-formation"),Q("ranching.q4","ranching.s1","word-choice","The family earned its income from ____ cattle in the high plains.",["ranching","rancid","ransacking"],"ranching","Ranching is the livestock-raising activity described.","word-choice")]});
D("rancho",{etymology:E("Borrowed from Spanish rancho, a farm or group of farm dwellings; it is related to the history of English ranch, which came through American Spanish. The word is used especially for farms or rough dwellings in Latin America and the Southwest.",null,null,null,"Etymonline, ranch (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ranch)."),contexts:[C("rancho.s1","歷史","The travelers spent the night at a rancho in northern Mexico, where the workers' adobe rooms stood beside the cattle pens.","旅人夜宿墨西哥北部的一座牧場，工人的土磚房就在牛欄旁邊。","Rancho can mean a cattle farm or a rough dwelling associated with workers there.","At a rancho identifies the lodging; where introduces the setting and the rooms' relation to the pens.","The place combines a working farm with basic workers' quarters.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The rancho was an ocean liner carrying passengers between two European ports.","The rancho was a farm and workers' dwelling in the American Southwest.","Rancho names a farm or associated dwelling, not a ship.")],quiz:[Q("rancho.q1","rancho.s1","meaning","In the American Southwest, a rancho may be a ___.",["cattle farm or workers' rough dwelling","formal court judgment","type of mathematical proof"],"cattle farm or workers' rough dwelling","The source sense covers a farm and its basic worker housing.","meaning"),Q("rancho.q2","rancho.s1","context","Where might a historical account mention a rancho?",["On a cattle property in northern Mexico","In a London theater's seating chart","In a laboratory's list of chemical units"],"On a cattle property in northern Mexico","Rancho is used for farms or dwellings in Latin America and the Southwest.","context"),Q("rancho.q3","rancho.s1","word-choice","The workers returned to the ____ after checking the cattle pens.",["rancho","rancid","rapacity"],"rancho","The rancho is the farm or workers' dwelling they returned to.","word-choice"),Q("rancho.q4","rancho.s1","confusable","Rancho is historically related to which English word?",["ranch","rancor","ransom"],"ranch","English ranch came through American Spanish rancho.","confusable")]});
D("rancid",{etymology:E("From Latin rancidus ‘rancid, stinking’, related to rancere ‘to stink’; the deeper origin of rancere is unknown. The English adjective is used especially of fats that have spoiled and developed a sour smell.",null,"rancere",null,"Etymonline, rancid (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rancid)."),contexts:[C("rancid.s1","食品","The cook threw away the rancid oil after its sharp sour smell lingered even when the bottle was closed.","即使瓶子蓋上後酸臭味仍揮之不去，廚師便把變質的油丟掉了。","Rancid describes fat or oil that has spoiled and smells sour or unpleasant.","Rancid modifies oil; after introduces the reason for discarding it.","The odor shows the oil has become spoiled.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The rancid butter smelled clean and sweet, so the baker used it to improve the cake.","The fresh butter smelled clean and sweet, so the baker used it to improve the cake.","Rancid fat has an unpleasant sour smell, not a clean sweet one.")],quiz:[Q("rancid.q1","rancid.s1","meaning","Rancid butter is butter that ___.",["has spoiled and smells unpleasant","has just been churned and smells fresh","has been frozen without changing"],"has spoiled and smells unpleasant","Rancid describes spoiled fats with a sour odor.","meaning"),Q("rancid.q2","rancid.s1","context","A bottle of oil has a sharp sour odor and tastes stale. It is probably ___.",["rancid","random","rampant"],"rancid","The sour smell is a sign of rancid oil.","context"),Q("rancid.q3","rancid.s1","word-choice","The chef replaced the ____ shortening before it ruined the pastries.",["rancid","ranked","rancorous"],"rancid","Spoiled shortening is rancid and has an unpleasant smell.","word-choice"),Q("rancid.q4","rancid.s1","meaning","Which item is most likely to become rancid?",["A bottle of old cooking oil","A new steel spoon","A dry paper label"],"A bottle of old cooking oil","Oils and other fats can spoil and turn rancid.","meaning")]});
D("rancor",{etymology:E("From Old French rancor ‘bitterness, resentment’, from Late Latin rancorem, which earlier referred to rancidness or a foul smell, from Latin rancere ‘stink’; the deeper Latin origin is unknown.",null,"rancere",null,"Etymonline, rancor (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rancor)."),contexts:[C("rancor.s1","政治","Years after the election, rancor between the two parties still blocked even routine budget talks.","選舉多年後，兩黨之間的積怨仍阻礙著例行預算協商。","Rancor is deep resentment or bitterness that is not easily forgiven.","Rancor is the subject; between identifies the parties, and still blocked gives its effect.","The long-lasting hostility prevents cooperation.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","There was rancor between the former rivals, but neither felt resentment and both had completely forgiven the other.","There was no rancor between the former rivals; both had forgiven each other and felt no resentment.","Rancor means persistent bitterness, so complete forgiveness and no resentment rule it out.")],quiz:[Q("rancor.q1","rancor.s1","meaning","Rancor between former allies is ___.",["deep, lasting resentment","a neutral random choice","a loud musical performance"],"deep, lasting resentment","Rancor is bitterness or hostility that persists.","meaning"),Q("rancor.q2","rancor.s1","context","Which scene shows rancor?",["Two colleagues still blame each other years after a dispute.","Two neighbors quickly forgive a small mistake.","A rancher checks a water trough."],"Two colleagues still blame each other years after a dispute.","Continuing blame years later shows deep resentment.","context"),Q("rancor.q3","rancor.s1","collocation","The court urged both sides to put aside their ____ and negotiate.",["rancor","rancidness","ranking"],"rancor","Rancor is the lasting bitterness the court asks them to set aside.","collocation"),Q("rancor.q4","rancor.s1","word-choice","The settlement ended the personal ____ that had divided the families.",["rancor","ranching","randomness"],"rancor","The word names persistent hostility between people.","word-choice")]});
D("rancorous",{etymology:E("From rancor + -ous, the adjective suffix meaning ‘full of or characterized by’; rancor passed through Old French from Late Latin rancor, ultimately related to Latin rancere ‘stink’, of unknown deeper origin.",null,"rancor","-ous","Etymonline, rancor (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rancor)."),contexts:[C("rancorous.s1","政治","The debate became rancorous when each speaker accused the other of deliberately betraying the public.","雙方發言者互相指控對方故意背叛民眾後，辯論變得充滿敵意。","Rancorous describes speech or relations marked by deep, lasting bitterness.","Rancorous modifies debate; when introduces the accusation that changed its tone.","The exchange is hostile and resentful rather than merely a calm disagreement.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Their rancorous reconciliation was warm, free of resentment, and followed by an apology from both sides.","Their amicable reconciliation was warm, free of resentment, and followed by an apology from both sides.","Rancorous means bitter or hostile, which conflicts with a warm and forgiving reconciliation.")],quiz:[Q("rancorous.q1","rancorous.s1","meaning","A rancorous argument is ___.",["bitter and hostile","quietly random","about spoiled cooking oil"],"bitter and hostile","Rancorous describes deep resentment in an exchange.","meaning"),Q("rancorous.q2","rancorous.s1","context","Which comment sounds rancorous?",["“I still resent how you blamed me, and I will not forget it.”","“We settled the matter and hold no grudge.”","“The sample was selected by chance.”"],"“I still resent how you blamed me, and I will not forget it.”","The speaker expresses lasting bitterness.","context"),Q("rancorous.q3","rancorous.s1","word-formation","Which noun is rancorous derived from?",["rancor","rancher","random"],"rancor","Rancorous is formed from rancor plus the adjective suffix -ous.","word-formation"),Q("rancorous.q4","rancorous.s1","word-choice","A ____ exchange continued long after the original disagreement had ended.",["rancorous","rancid","rampant"],"rancorous","Lasting bitterness makes rancorous the correct adjective.","word-choice")]});
D("random",{etymology:E("From Anglo-French randon ‘impetuosity, speed’, from Old French randir ‘run, gallop’; the later sense ‘without a plan or predictable pattern’ developed from the idea of acting at random.",null,"randir",null,"Etymonline, random (https://www.etymonline.com/word/random)."),contexts:[C("random.s1","統計","The researcher used a random sample by drawing thirty patient numbers from a computer-generated list.","研究人員從電腦產生的名單中抽出三十個病患編號，組成隨機樣本。","Random means chosen by chance rather than by a deliberate pattern.","Random modifies sample; by introduces the chance-based selection method.","Each patient number had a chance of selection instead of being chosen by a fixed rule.") ,C("random.s2","行為","The guard made a random search of the bags, opening them without selecting any by size or owner.","警衛胡亂檢查行李，沒有按大小或所有者挑選。","Random can mean done without a clear aim or careful selection.","Random modifies search; without explains the lack of a selection rule.","The search is unsystematic rather than governed by a stated criterion.") ,C("random.s3","口語","It was random that our dentist and my old piano teacher turned out to be cousins.","原來牙醫和我以前的鋼琴老師是表親，這件事真出乎意料。","Informally, random can mean odd or unexpected.","Random is a predicative adjective after was; that-clause states the surprising coincidence.","The relationship feels unexpected and unrelated to the speaker's plans.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The survey used a random sample by interviewing only the first thirty people who entered the same classroom.","The survey used a convenient sample by interviewing the first thirty people who entered that classroom.","Choosing everyone from one fixed entrance group is systematic convenience sampling, not selection by chance.")],quiz:[Q("random.q1","random.s1","meaning","A random sample is selected ___.",["by chance rather than a fixed preference","only from the researcher's friends","in alphabetical order every time"],"by chance rather than a fixed preference","Random selection avoids choosing participants by a deliberate pattern.","meaning"),Q("random.q2","random.s2","context","A guard conducts a random search. What does that suggest?",["The bags are checked without a clear selection pattern.","Every bag is sorted by owner and color.","Only bags with a printed label are checked."],"The bags are checked without a clear selection pattern.","This sense describes an unsystematic search.","context"),Q("random.q3","random.s3","register","In casual speech, “That was random!” often means it was ___.",["unexpected or oddly unrelated","chosen by a scientific lottery","rancid"],"unexpected or oddly unrelated","The informal sense describes something surprising or out of place.","register"),Q("random.q4","random.s1","word-choice","To avoid bias, the team assigned each file a number and picked a ____ set using a random-number generator.",["random","rancorous","rancid"],"random","The generator selects by chance, so random fits.","word-choice")]});
D("randomly",{etymology:E("Formed from random + -ly, the regular adverb suffix; random entered English through Anglo-French randon, originally ‘impetuosity, speed’, before developing the chance-based sense.",null,"random","-ly","Etymonline, random (https://www.etymonline.com/word/random)."),contexts:[C("randomly.s1","研究","The software randomly assigned each volunteer to one of two treatment groups, so neither the patients nor the staff chose the group.","軟體把每位志願者隨機分派到兩個治療組之一，因此病患和工作人員都沒有自行挑選組別。","Randomly means according to chance rather than a planned selection.","Randomly modifies assigned; so explains how chance assignment prevents personal choice.","The software uses chance instead of letting people select a group.") ,C("randomly.s2","行為","He opened drawers randomly, looking for the missing key without following a list or any order.","他沒有依照清單或順序，而是胡亂打開抽屜尋找遺失的鑰匙。","Randomly can mean without aim or a clear purpose.","Randomly modifies opened; without introduces the lack of an ordered plan.","The search is haphazard rather than systematic.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The cards were dealt randomly in the same fixed order every time, with no shuffle or chance involved.","The cards were dealt systematically in the same fixed order every time, with no shuffle or chance involved.","A fixed repeated order is systematic; randomly means chance determines the order.")],quiz:[Q("randomly.q1","randomly.s1","meaning","If names are selected randomly, they are selected ___.",["by chance","according to height only","from the last page every time"],"by chance","Randomly describes a chance-based choice.","meaning"),Q("randomly.q2","randomly.s2","context","Which person searched randomly?",["She opened drawers without a plan, hoping to find the key.","He checked each drawer from left to right using a list.","They searched only the labeled desk."],"She opened drawers without a plan, hoping to find the key.","The action is haphazard and has no clear order.","context"),Q("randomly.q3","randomly.s1","word-form","Choose the adverb: “The app paired users ___.”",["randomly","random","randomness"],"randomly","Randomly modifies the verb paired.","word form"),Q("randomly.q4","randomly.s2","confusable","Which phrase means “without a clear aim”?",["The papers were scattered randomly.","The sample was selected randomly by a lottery.","The names were chosen randomly by software."],"The papers were scattered randomly.","Scattering without a plan is the haphazard sense; lottery selection is chance-based.","confusable")]});
D("range",{etymology:E("From Old French range, a row or line, from ranger ‘arrange, set in order’; the French word is related to Germanic forms for a row or ring, though the deeper route is not certain. Senses extended to limits, distance, mountains, and movement.",null,"ranger",null,"Etymonline, range (https://www.etymonline.com/word/range)."),contexts:[C("range.s1","購物","The clinic stocks a range of inhalers, from compact models for travel to larger devices with dose counters.","診所備有各種吸入器，從旅行用的輕巧款到附劑量計數器的較大型裝置都有。","A range is the limits or variety available within a set.","Range is the object of stocks; of inhalers specifies the items, and from-to gives the variety.","Several models are available across different features and uses.") ,C("range.s2","工程","The radio has a range of twenty kilometres in open country, but buildings reduce its reach.","這台無線電在空曠地區的有效距離為二十公里，但建築物會縮短訊號範圍。","Range can mean the distance over which a device is effective.","Range follows has; of twenty kilometres measures the distance, while but contrasts obstructed conditions.","The signal reaches about twenty kilometres where obstacles are absent.") ,C("range.s3","地理","A snow-covered mountain range separated the coastal villages from the inland plateau.","一列覆雪山脈把沿海村莊與內陸高原隔開。","A range is a line or chain of mountains.","Range is modified by mountain; separated states its relation to the villages and plateau.","The peaks form an extended chain across the landscape.") ,C("range.s4","數據","Temperatures range from 4°C at dawn to 19°C in the afternoon.","氣溫從黎明時的攝氏四度到下午的十九度不等。","As a verb, range can vary between two limits or include a variety.","Range is followed by from and to to state lower and upper limits.","The temperature changes within the stated endpoints.") ,C("range.s5","生態","The wolves range across the northern forest, following herds as the seasons change.","狼群在北方森林中四處活動，隨季節變化追蹤獸群。","As a verb, range can mean move freely over an area.","Range is intransitive with across introducing the area; following gives the animals' movement pattern.","The wolves roam over a broad habitat rather than staying in one place.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The readings ranged 4°C to 19°C during the day.","The readings ranged from 4°C to 19°C during the day.","When range states two limits, the standard pattern is range from one value to another.")],quiz:[Q("range.q1","range.s1","meaning","A store's range of coats is its ___.",["variety of coats available","distance its radio signal travels","chain of mountains"],"variety of coats available","Range can mean the selection or variety offered.","meaning"),Q("range.q2","range.s2","context","A walkie-talkie's range is five kilometres. What does that tell you?",["How far its signal can work","How many colours it comes in","How tall the nearest mountain is"],"How far its signal can work","Range is the effective distance of the signal.","context"),Q("range.q3","range.s4","grammar","Choose the standard construction.",["Prices range from $8 to $25.","Prices range $8 until $25.","Prices range between $8 to $25."],"Prices range from $8 to $25.","Use range from a lower limit to an upper limit.","grammar"),Q("range.q4","range.s5","meaning","If deer range across a valley, they ___.",["move freely over the area","are ranked by size","are held for ransom"],"move freely over the area","The verb range can mean roam across a region.","meaning")]});
D("rank",{etymology:E("The noun rank ‘row, line, position’ came through French rang from Germanic forms related to Proto-Germanic *hringaz ‘ring, circle’; the verb developed from placing in ranks. The adjective rank ‘foul, luxuriant’ has a separate Old English history.",null,"hringaz / ranc",null,"Etymonline, rank (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rank)."),contexts:[C("rank.s1","軍事","After twenty years of service, the officer reached the rank of colonel and took command of the base.","服役二十年後，這名軍官升至上校軍階，並接掌基地指揮。","Rank is a position in an organisation, especially a military grade.","Rank is the object of reached; of colonel names the position attained.","Colonel is the officer's formal military grade.") ,C("rank.s2","組織","The volunteers stood in ranks outside the hall while the coordinator checked attendance.","志工在大廳外排成一列列，協調員則點名確認出席。","Ranks can mean lines or rows of people; the plural ranks can also mean ordinary members of a group.","In ranks describes the arrangement; while links it to the attendance check.","The volunteers are arranged in rows.") ,C("rank.s3","評比","The magazine ranked the five designs by durability, placing the strongest sample first.","雜誌依耐用度替五款設計排名，把最耐用的樣品排在第一。","As a verb, rank means assign a position on a scale or list.","Ranked takes designs as object; by gives the criterion and placing states the result.","The designs receive relative positions according to durability.") ,C("rank.s4","植物","Rank weeds filled the untended garden, growing thickly and giving off a sour smell.","雜草在無人照料的花園裡長得過於茂盛，還散發出酸臭味。","The adjective rank can describe foul-smelling or excessively luxuriant growth.","Rank modifies weeds; growing and giving off add the physical signs.","The weeds are both overgrown and unpleasant-smelling.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The committee ranked the three finalists from their writing samples first to third place.","The committee ranked the three finalists from first to third place based on their writing samples.","Rank takes the people or items as its object and assigns them positions; place the ranking scale after the object.")],quiz:[Q("rank.q1","rank.s1","meaning","An officer's rank is the officer's ___.",["position or grade in the organisation","loud complaint","ability to grow in a garden"],"position or grade in the organisation","Rank names a position, especially in the armed forces.","meaning"),Q("rank.q2","rank.s2","context","“The ordinary ranks supported the captain” refers to ___.",["the regular members below the officers","a list of mountain ranges","a foul odor"],"the regular members below the officers","Ranks can refer collectively to ordinary members of a group.","context"),Q("rank.q3","rank.s3","grammar","Which sentence uses rank as a verb?",["The judges ranked each entry by originality.","She held the rank of captain.","Rank weeds covered the path."],"The judges ranked each entry by originality.","Ranked takes each entry as its object and assigns a position.","grammar"),Q("rank.q4","rank.s4","meaning","Rank weeds are weeds that ___.",["grow thickly or smell unpleasant","have been officially ordered by a judge","were selected by chance"],"grow thickly or smell unpleasant","The adjective rank can mean excessively luxuriant or foul-smelling.","meaning")]});
D("ranker",{etymology:E("From rank + -er, naming a person in a rank; in military English, a ranker is an enlisted soldier who is not an officer, especially one beginning at the lowest rank.",null,"rank","-er","Etymonline, rank (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rank)."),contexts:[C("ranker.s1","軍事","The young ranker learned field procedures from a sergeant before joining the patrol.","這名年輕列兵先跟著中士學習野外程序，之後才加入巡邏隊。","A ranker is an enlisted soldier, commonly one of the lower ranks.","Ranker is the subject; learned and joining describe the soldier's training and next step.","The recruit is a non-officer serving in the enlisted ranks.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The ranker commanded every general in the army as its highest-ranking officer.","The ranker served as an enlisted soldier under the command of officers.","Ranker refers to an enlisted soldier, not the highest-ranking officer.")],quiz:[Q("ranker.q1","ranker.s1","meaning","A ranker in military usage is generally ___.",["an enlisted soldier, not an officer","the highest-ranking general","a civilian who sells uniforms"],"an enlisted soldier, not an officer","Ranker commonly refers to a soldier in the enlisted ranks.","meaning"),Q("ranker.q2","ranker.s1","context","Who is most likely the ranker in a unit report?",["A newly enlisted private learning from a sergeant","The elected mayor visiting the base","The general signing the report"],"A newly enlisted private learning from a sergeant","The private is an enlisted soldier and fits the source sense.","context"),Q("ranker.q3","ranker.s1","word-formation","Which base word forms ranker?",["rank","rancor","ranch"],"rank","Ranker is formed from rank with the person suffix -er.","word-formation"),Q("ranker.q4","ranker.s1","word-choice","The experienced sergeant taught the new ____ how to pack for patrol.",["ranker","ranking","rankness"],"ranker","The sentence needs a person serving as an enlisted soldier.","word-choice")]});
D("ranking",{etymology:E("From rank + -ing, the noun-forming ending; ranking names an assigned position in a list or order, especially for players, schools, or institutions.",null,"rank","-ing","Etymonline, rank (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rank)."),contexts:[C("ranking.s1","教育","The university improved its national ranking after publishing graduation rates and research data for independent review.","這所大學公布畢業率與研究資料供外部審查後，全國排名有所提升。","A ranking is a position in an ordered list, often comparing institutions or competitors.","Ranking is the object of improved; after gives the action preceding the higher position.","The university moved upward relative to other institutions.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The published ranking listed every school alphabetically and gave none of them a comparative position.","The published directory listed every school alphabetically and gave none a comparative position.","A ranking assigns comparative positions; an alphabetical directory without positions is not a ranking.")],quiz:[Q("ranking.q1","ranking.s1","meaning","A team's ranking tells you ___.",["its position relative to other teams","the team's ranch location","the number of ransoms paid"],"its position relative to other teams","A ranking places teams in an ordered comparison.","meaning"),Q("ranking.q2","ranking.s1","context","A school moves from 18th to 12th in a ranking. What happened?",["Its relative position improved.","It became a mountain range.","It was selected at random."],"Its relative position improved.","A smaller ordinal number indicates a higher position in the list.","context"),Q("ranking.q3","ranking.s1","word-formation","Ranking is built from which verb or noun?",["rank","ransom","rant"],"rank","The noun ranking adds -ing to rank.","word-formation"),Q("ranking.q4","ranking.s1","word-choice","The sports site updated the players' ____ after the tournament.",["ranking","rancor","ranching"],"ranking","The list of relative positions is a ranking.","word-choice")]});
D("ransack",{etymology:E("From Old Norse rannsaka ‘search a house’, a compound of rann ‘house’ and saka ‘search, examine’; English uses it for a rough, thorough search that may involve stealing or disorder.",null,"rann + saka",null,"Etymonline, ransack (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ransack)."),contexts:[C("ransack.s1","犯罪","The burglars ransacked the cottage, opening cupboards and emptying drawers while searching for jewelry.","竊賊洗劫小屋，打開櫥櫃、倒空抽屜尋找珠寶。","To ransack a place is to search it roughly and thoroughly, often while stealing.","Ransacked takes cottage as its object; the participles give the disorderly search actions.","The burglars search many parts of the home and leave things disturbed.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The burglars ransacked the study but left every drawer closed and every book in its original place.","The burglars searched the study thoroughly, opening drawers and scattering books as they looked for valuables.","Ransack implies a rough, thorough search, so an untouched room does not fit.")],quiz:[Q("ransack.q1","ransack.s1","meaning","If thieves ransack a room, they ___.",["search it roughly and thoroughly","paint it without entering","rank its furniture by price"],"search it roughly and thoroughly","Ransack means search a place thoroughly, often leaving disorder.","meaning"),Q("ransack.q2","ransack.s1","context","Which report describes a ransacked office?",["Files and drawers were scattered while someone searched for cash.","Every desk remained untouched and locked.","The staff lined up neatly for a photograph."],"Files and drawers were scattered while someone searched for cash.","A disorderly thorough search is characteristic of ransacking.","context"),Q("ransack.q3","ransack.s1","word-choice","Investigators found that someone had ____ the cabinet for documents.",["ransacked","ranked","rancid"],"ransacked","The cabinet was searched thoroughly and roughly.","word-choice"),Q("ransack.q4","ransack.s1","etymology","The Old Norse parts of ransack referred to a house and to ___.",["searching or examining","promoting a policy","raising cattle"],"searching or examining","The source compound combines rann ‘house’ and saka ‘search, examine’.","meaning")]});
D("ransom",{etymology:E("From Old French rançon, from Latin redemptio ‘redemption, buying back’; the word names money paid or demanded for a captive's release and also the act of releasing a captive by payment.",null,"redemptio",null,"Etymonline, ransom (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ransom)."),contexts:[C("ransom.s1","犯罪","The kidnappers demanded a ransom of two million dollars in exchange for the journalist's release.","綁匪要求兩百萬美元贖金，才肯釋放這名記者。","A ransom is money demanded to free someone held by force.","Ransom is the object of demanded; of two million dollars gives the amount, and in exchange states the condition.","The money is requested as the price for releasing the captive.") ,C("ransom.s2","犯罪","The family ransomed the sailor by paying the amount specified in the pirates' message.","家人支付海盜訊息中指定的金額，贖回了這名水手。","To ransom someone can mean free a captive by paying money.","Ransomed takes sailor as its object; by introduces the payment method.","The family pays to secure the sailor's release.") ,C("ransom.s3","犯罪","The gang ransomed the aid worker and threatened to keep her unless the charity paid.","該團夥綁架並挾持援助工作者，威脅慈善組織付錢，否則就不放人。","To ransom can also mean hold a person and demand money for release.","Ransomed takes aid worker as its object; unless introduces the ransom condition.","The gang holds the captive while demanding payment.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The gang released the captive without requesting payment, calling the unpaid release a ransom.","The gang released the captive without requesting payment, so it was an unconditional release, not a ransom.","Ransom is payment demanded for release; an unconditional release with no demand is not a ransom.")],quiz:[Q("ransom.q1","ransom.s1","meaning","A ransom is money demanded ___.",["in exchange for freeing a captive","to publish a book proof","to rank a list"],"in exchange for freeing a captive","The noun names payment demanded for a hostage's release.","meaning"),Q("ransom.q2","ransom.s2","context","The family ransomed the sailor. What did they do?",["Paid to secure the sailor's freedom","Held the sailor and demanded money","Ranked the sailor among officers"],"Paid to secure the sailor's freedom","The verb in this sense means free a captive by paying.","context"),Q("ransom.q3","ransom.s3","context","The kidnappers ransomed a tourist and sent a payment demand. What was their action?",["They held the tourist while demanding money for release.","They paid to free the tourist from captivity.","They returned the tourist without a demand."],"They held the tourist while demanding money for release.","This verb sense means hold a person and ask for payment to release them.","context"),Q("ransom.q4","ransom.s1","word-choice","The family delivered the demanded ____ so the hostage could come home.",["ransom","ranking","rancor"],"ransom","The payment demanded for release is a ransom.","word-choice")]});
D("rant",{etymology:E("Probably from Dutch ranten ‘talk nonsense, rave’; the precise deeper origin is uncertain. English rant came to mean speaking at length and angrily, and the same form can name such a speech.",null,"ranten",null,"Etymonline, rant (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rant)."),contexts:[C("rant.s1","日常","The caller ranted for ten minutes about the delayed train, repeating the same accusation at full volume.","來電者針對火車誤點怒斥了十分鐘，還大聲重複同一項指責。","To rant is to speak angrily at length, often with more force than the facts warrant.","Ranted is followed by for ten minutes to show duration; about introduces the topic.","The caller's speech is prolonged and angry rather than a brief complaint.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","He went rant about the parking fee for half an hour.","He went on a rant about the parking fee for half an hour.","Use go on a rant for the noun phrase, or say he ranted about the fee; went rant is not grammatical.")],quiz:[Q("rant.q1","rant.s1","meaning","A person who rants is usually ___.",["speaking angrily and at length","selecting names by chance","proofreading quietly"],"speaking angrily and at length","Rant describes an extended, forceful complaint or speech.","meaning"),Q("rant.q2","rant.s1","context","Which scene includes a rant?",["A passenger loudly complains for twenty minutes about a canceled flight.","A clerk calmly confirms one travel time.","A rancher checks a water trough."],"A passenger loudly complains for twenty minutes about a canceled flight.","The complaint is both prolonged and angry.","context"),Q("rant.q3","rant.s1","grammar","Choose the standard noun phrase.",["She went on a rant about the noise.","She went rant about the noise.","She went to ranting about the noise."],"She went on a rant about the noise.","The noun construction is go on a rant; the verb construction is simply rant about.","grammar"),Q("rant.q4","rant.s1","word-choice","The coach began to ____ when the team ignored the safety rules again.",["rant","ransack","ransom"],"rant","An angry extended speech fits rant.","word-choice")]});
D("rap",{etymology:E("The quick-knock verb is a Germanic echoic word recorded in Middle English, perhaps influenced by Old Norse klappa; the noun for a knock came from it. The music and blame/charge senses developed later from separate uses of the same form.",null,null,null,"Etymonline, rap (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rap)."),contexts:[C("rap.s1","日常","She gave the metal door a quick rap with her knuckles, and the caretaker opened it from inside.","她用指節快速敲了金屬門一下，管理員便從裡面把門打開。","A rap is a quick, sharp knock.","Rap is the object of gave; with her knuckles states the means.","The sound is one short sharp knock.") ,C("rap.s2","音樂","The documentary traces how rap grew from rhythmic spoken lyrics at neighborhood gatherings into a global music form.","這部紀錄片追溯說唱音樂如何從社區聚會中的節奏口語歌詞，發展成全球性的音樂形式。","Rap is popular music in which words are spoken or chanted in rhythm.","Rap is the subject; how introduces the development being traced.","The word names the music genre, not the knocking sound.") ,C("rap.s3","法律","After the evidence cleared him, Malik was relieved to escape the rap for the warehouse theft.","證據證明馬利克清白後，他終於鬆了一口氣，不再背負倉庫竊案的指控。","Informally, a rap can mean blame or a criminal charge.","Rap follows the phrase escape the; for identifies the alleged offense.","The word refers to an accusation rather than a knock or music.") ,C("rap.s4","通用","The impatient customer rapped twice on the counter to get the clerk's attention.","不耐煩的顧客在櫃檯上敲了兩下，要引起店員注意。","As a verb, rap means hit a surface quickly and sharply.","Rapped takes on the counter as its surface complement; twice gives the number of taps.","The action makes two quick sharp knocks.") ,C("rap.s5","音樂","The poet rapped a verse over a steady drum loop while the audience clapped to the beat.","詩人在穩定的鼓聲伴奏上節奏化地說出一段詩句，觀眾則跟著節拍鼓掌。","As a verb, rap can mean perform rhythmic spoken lyrics.","Rapped takes verse as object; over introduces the musical backing.","The poet delivers words rhythmically over a beat.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","I heard rap at the apartment door, so I went to answer it.","I heard a rap at the apartment door, so I went to answer it.","The countable noun for one quick knock needs an article in this singular construction.")],quiz:[Q("rap.q1","rap.s1","meaning","A rap at the door is ___.",["a quick, sharp knock","a long mountain chain","a money demand for a hostage"],"a quick, sharp knock","The noun rap can name one brief knock.","meaning"),Q("rap.q2","rap.s2","context","A playlist lists rap alongside jazz and reggae. Here rap is ___.",["rhythmic spoken-word music","a criminal charge","a tap on wood"],"rhythmic spoken-word music","The musical sense is a genre built around rhythmic spoken lyrics.","context"),Q("rap.q3","rap.s3","meaning","To escape the rap for a theft means to avoid ___.",["blame or a criminal charge","a sharp knock","performing a song"],"blame or a criminal charge","Informal rap can mean an accusation or charge.","meaning"),Q("rap.q4","rap.s4","grammar","Choose the correct past-tense sentence.",["She rapped twice on the window.","She rap twice on the window yesterday.","She rapped to the window twice on."],"She rapped twice on the window.","The verb takes the surface with on; rapped is its regular past form.","grammar")]});
D("rapacious",{etymology:E("From Latin rapax, genitive rapacis ‘grasping, plundering’, from rapere ‘seize, carry off’; the adjective describes greedy taking or predatory exploitation.",null,"rapere",null,"Etymonline, rapacity (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rapacity)."),contexts:[C("rapacious.s1","商業","The investor's rapacious appetite for profit led him to buy every available apartment and raise rents sharply.","這名投資者對利潤貪得無厭，買下所有可售公寓並大幅提高租金。","Rapacious can mean extremely greedy for money, food, or power.","Rapacious modifies appetite; for identifies what is greedily desired, and led introduces its consequence.","The investor tries to acquire more property and income without restraint.") ,C("rapacious.s2","社會","The report called the illegal lender rapacious because he trapped families in debt and seized their homes.","報告稱這名非法放貸者掠奪成性，因為他讓家庭陷入債務，還奪走他們的房屋。","Rapacious can describe someone who lives by robbing or exploiting others.","Rapacious modifies lender; because introduces the exploitative conduct supporting that judgment.","The lender gains wealth by taking advantage of vulnerable families.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The rapacious landlord returned every overpayment, lowered all rents, and refused to take any profit.","The generous landlord returned every overpayment, lowered all rents, and refused to take any profit.","Rapacious describes greedy or exploitative taking, which conflicts with returning money and refusing profit.")],quiz:[Q("rapacious.q1","rapacious.s1","meaning","A rapacious appetite for wealth is ___.",["an extreme and greedy desire for wealth","a random choice of a number","a sour smell from old oil"],"an extreme and greedy desire for wealth","Rapacious describes greed and a desire to seize more than is fair.","meaning"),Q("rapacious.q2","rapacious.s2","context","Which person is rapacious in the predatory sense?",["A lender takes homes through deceptive debt terms.","A donor gives food to families in need.","A clerk returns a lost wallet untouched."],"A lender takes homes through deceptive debt terms.","The lender exploits vulnerable people for gain.","context"),Q("rapacious.q3","rapacious.s1","word-choice","The ____ collector demanded more land and money despite already owning half the valley.",["rapacious","rancid","ranching"],"rapacious","The collector's excessive desire to seize wealth is rapacious.","word-choice"),Q("rapacious.q4","rapacious.s2","confusable","What makes an act rapacious rather than merely profitable?",["It involves greedy seizure or exploitation.","It is selected by chance.","It is a brief knock at a door."],"It involves greedy seizure or exploitation.","Rapacious has a strongly predatory, exploitative sense.","confusable")]});
D("rapacity",{etymology:E("From French rapacité and Latin rapacitatem, from rapax ‘grasping, plundering’, from rapere ‘seize’; rapacity is the quality or practice of taking wealth or goods greedily and unfairly.",null,"rapere","-ity","Etymonline, rapacity (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rapacity)."),contexts:[C("rapacity.s1","財經","The inquiry exposed the contractor's rapacity: he inflated invoices and took public funds meant for school repairs.","調查揭露承包商的貪婪掠奪：他虛報帳單，侵吞原本用於學校修繕的公款。","Rapacity is fierce greed shown by taking more wealth or property than is fair.","Rapacity follows exposed; the colon introduces the concrete evidence of the greed.","The contractor diverts public money for personal gain.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The mayor's rapacity was praised because she refused all gifts, repaid public funds, and reduced her own salary.","The mayor's integrity was praised because she refused all gifts, repaid public funds, and reduced her own salary.","Rapacity means greedy taking; the described honesty and self-restraint show the opposite.")],quiz:[Q("rapacity.q1","rapacity.s1","meaning","Rapacity is ___.",["greedy or predatory taking","a measured range of temperatures","the sound of one knock"],"greedy or predatory taking","The noun names the quality of taking wealth or goods greedily.","meaning"),Q("rapacity.q2","rapacity.s1","context","An audit reveals a director diverted money from workers' wages into a private account. This is evidence of ___.",["rapacity","ranching","randomness"],"rapacity","The director is seizing funds unfairly for personal gain.","context"),Q("rapacity.q3","rapacity.s1","word-formation","Rapacity is the noun related to which adjective?",["rapacious","rampant","rancid"],"rapacious","Rapacity names the quality of being rapacious.","word-formation"),Q("rapacity.q4","rapacity.s1","word-choice","The inquiry condemned the official's ____ in taking fees from every applicant.",["rapacity","rapport","rapidity"],"rapacity","Taking excessive fees from applicants shows greedy exploitation.","word-choice")]});
