(function(){const RA=globalThis.RA,D=(l,p)=>RA.D(l,p),E=(origin,prefix,root,suffix,source)=>({origin,prefix,root,suffix,source}),C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:"authored"}),M=(errorType,wrong,right,reason)=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason}),Q=(id,senseId,type,prompt,options,answer,explain,errorType)=>({id,senseId,type,prompt,options,answer,explain,errorType});
D("ravine",{etymology:E("From French ravin ‘gully’, from Old French raviner ‘sweep down, cascade; pillage’, ultimately Latin rapina ‘robbery, plundering’; the landform sense was influenced by the rush of water through a gorge.",null,"rapina",null,"Etymonline, ravine (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ravine)."),contexts:[C("ravine.s1","地理","The footpath crossed a narrow ravine on a wooden bridge, with steep rock walls dropping to a stream below.","小徑以木橋橫越一道狹窄深谷，兩側陡峭岩壁下方有溪流。","A ravine is a deep, narrow valley with steep sides.","Ravine is the object of crossed; with introduces details of its steep sides and stream.","The narrow valley has sharply descending sides and a stream at its bottom.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The survey marked a broad, level plain with no slope or depression as a ravine.","The survey marked the deep, narrow valley with steep sides as a ravine.","A ravine is a deep narrow valley with steep sides, not a flat plain.")],quiz:[Q("ravine.q1","ravine.s1","meaning","A ravine is a ___.",["deep narrow valley with steep sides","wide level field","man-made water tank"],"deep narrow valley with steep sides","That is the source definition of ravine.","meaning"),Q("ravine.q2","ravine.s1","context","Which landscape is most likely a ravine?",["A stream lies between steep, close-set rock walls.","A flat meadow stretches without a slope.","A hill has a broad rounded top."],"A stream lies between steep, close-set rock walls.","The narrow valley and steep sides identify a ravine.","context"),Q("ravine.q3","ravine.s1","collocation","The hikers descended into a deep ____ after the rain.",["ravine","rationale","rayon"],"ravine","Deep ravine is a natural collocation for a steep-sided valley.","collocation"),Q("ravine.q4","ravine.s1","word-choice","A narrow valley cut sharply into the hillside is a ____. ",["ravine","rattle","raven"],"ravine","The landform described is a deep narrow valley.","word-choice")]});
D("ravish",{etymology:E("From Old French raviss-, stem of ravir ‘seize, carry off hastily’, from Vulgar Latin *rapire and Latin rapere ‘seize and carry away’; English also developed figurative delight and an older legal sexual-violence sense.",null,"rapere",null,"Etymonline, ravish (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ravish)."),contexts:[C("ravish.s1","文學","The violin solo ravished the audience, leaving several listeners quietly moved by its final passage.","小提琴獨奏使聽眾深深陶醉，最後一段令幾位聽眾默默動容。","To ravish can mean to fill someone with great delight.","Ravished takes the audience as its object; leaving describes the resulting state.","The music gives the listeners intense pleasure and emotion."),C("ravish.s2","歷史","The old chronicle says raiders ravished the village's stores, carrying off grain and tools during the retreat.","古編年史記載，襲擊者在撤退時掠走村中糧食與工具。","In literary or historical use, to ravish can mean seize and carry away by force.","Ravished takes stores as its object; carrying off explains the seizure.","The passage explicitly describes goods being taken by force."),C("ravish.s3","法律史","A legal historian notes that an old statute used ravish for the crime of forcing sex on a person; modern writing uses more direct legal terminology.","法律史學者指出，舊法規曾以 ravish 指強迫他人發生性行為的犯罪；現代寫作使用更直接的法律用語。","In old legal use, ravish meant to force sex on someone; this sense is now archaic.","Used ravish for the crime introduces a historical term; the semicolon distinguishes modern usage.","The sentence explicitly locates this definition in old legal language.")],mistakes:[M("register","The modern consent policy describes the assault as “ravishing” to sound neutral and current.","The modern consent policy describes the assault with direct, current legal terminology.","Ravish for sexual assault is an archaic legal usage; using it as neutral contemporary terminology is inappropriate and unclear.")],quiz:[Q("ravish.q1","ravish.s1","meaning","If a performance ravishes its audience in the figurative sense, it ___.",["fills them with great delight","takes their belongings by force","makes a chemical change"],"fills them with great delight","This sense means to delight or enchant deeply.","meaning"),Q("ravish.q2","ravish.s2","context","In a historical account, raiders ravished the granary and carried away its grain. They ___.",["seized and took the grain by force","admired the grain's flavor","approved the grain for sale"],"seized and took the grain by force","The context supplies the older literary sense of forceful seizure.","context"),Q("ravish.q3","ravish.s3","register","How should ravish meaning sexual assault be treated in present-day writing?",["As an archaic historical/legal term; use clear current terminology.","As a neutral everyday synonym for delight.","As the standard name of a plant."],"As an archaic historical/legal term; use clear current terminology.","This source sense is explicitly marked old legal use.","register"),Q("ravish.q4","ravish.s1","word-choice","The moving aria seemed to ____ the listeners with delight.",["ravish","ratify","reabsorb"],"ravish","The figurative verb means to fill someone with great delight.","word-choice")]});
D("raw",{etymology:E("From Old English hreaw ‘uncooked’, from Proto-Germanic *khrawaz and PIE *kreue- ‘raw flesh’; later senses extend to untreated materials, sore skin, and inexperienced people.",null,"*khrawaz",null,"Etymonline, raw (https://www.etymonline.com/word/raw)."),contexts:[C("raw.s1","飲食","The chef kept the raw fish chilled on ice and cooked each portion only after the guests ordered.","廚師將生魚放在冰上冷藏，等客人點餐後才烹調各份料理。","Raw means not cooked.","Raw modifies fish; and links the storage practice to the later cooking.","The fish has not yet been cooked when it is kept on ice."),C("raw.s2","製造","The mill buys raw cotton before spinning it into thread and weaving the thread into cloth.","紡織廠在棉花尚未加工前購入，之後再紡成線並織成布。","Raw means in a natural state, not yet treated or manufactured.","Raw modifies cotton; before and into show the stages of processing.","The cotton is the unprocessed input material."),C("raw.s3","健康","The skin on his heel was raw after the new boots rubbed against it during the long walk.","長途步行時新靴子摩擦腳跟，使那裡的皮膚擦紅而刺痛。","Raw can describe skin that is red and sore because it has been rubbed.","Raw is a subject complement after was; after explains the cause.","Repeated friction left the skin sore and abraded."),C("raw.s4","職場","The raw recruit shadowed an experienced technician for a month before handling the equipment alone.","這名缺乏經驗的新進人員先跟隨資深技術員一個月，之後才獨自操作設備。","Raw can mean new to a job and not yet skilled.","Raw modifies recruit; before marks the training that preceded independent work.","The recruit needs training before working independently.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The chef served raw chicken after roasting it thoroughly to a safe temperature.","The chef served cooked chicken after roasting it thoroughly to a safe temperature.","Raw means not cooked, so thoroughly roasted chicken is cooked, not raw.")],quiz:[Q("raw.q1","raw.s1","meaning","Raw vegetables are vegetables that are ___.",["not cooked","already roasted","made from animal skin"],"not cooked","Raw in food means uncooked.","meaning"),Q("raw.q2","raw.s2","context","Which is a raw material?",["cotton before it is spun into thread","a finished cotton shirt","a woven bedsheet"],"cotton before it is spun into thread","It has not yet been manufactured into a textile.","context"),Q("raw.q3","raw.s3","meaning","If a blister breaks and the skin underneath is raw, it is ___.",["red and sore","fully healed and insensitive","untrained for a job"],"red and sore","The skin sense means rubbed, tender, or abraded.","meaning"),Q("raw.q4","raw.s4","context","A raw employee who needs close supervision is ___.",["new and not yet skilled","made from unprocessed cotton","served uncooked"],"new and not yet skilled","Raw can describe someone inexperienced in a job.","context")]});
D("rawhide",{etymology:E("A compound recorded in the 1650s from raw + hide: hide is the skin of a large animal, while raw specifies that the skin has not been tanned.",null,"hide","compound","Etymonline, rawhide (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rawhide)."),contexts:[C("rawhide.s1","製革","The craft worker soaked the rawhide before shaping it into a drumhead, since the untreated cow skin was stiff when dry.","工匠先浸泡生皮，再將它製成鼓面，因為未處理的牛皮乾燥時很硬。","Rawhide is untanned animal skin, especially cow skin, used for durable goods.","Rawhide is the object of soaked; before and since explain preparation and material condition.","The material is untreated hide that softens when soaked before shaping.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The saddle maker chose rawhide that had been fully tanned, dyed, and softened into finished leather.","The saddle maker chose untanned rawhide before treating it into finished leather.","Rawhide specifically means hide before tanning, rather than already finished leather.")],quiz:[Q("rawhide.q1","rawhide.s1","meaning","Rawhide is animal skin that has not yet been ___.",["tanned","woven into cotton","cooked"],"tanned","Rawhide is untanned hide.","meaning"),Q("rawhide.q2","rawhide.s1","context","Which item could be made from rawhide?",["a tough cord made from untreated cow skin","a rayon shirt","a cooked meal"],"a tough cord made from untreated cow skin","Untanned cow skin can be used for ropes and durable goods.","context"),Q("rawhide.q3","rawhide.s1","word-formation","The compound rawhide combines raw with ___.",["hide, meaning animal skin","height, meaning measurement","hive, meaning bee home"],"hide, meaning animal skin","Raw describes the untreated state of the hide.","word-formation"),Q("rawhide.q4","rawhide.s1","word-choice","Before tanning, the craftsman cut the cow's ____ into narrow strips.",["rawhide","rayon","readability"],"rawhide","Untanned cow skin is rawhide.","word-choice")]});
D("ray",{etymology:E("From Old French rai ‘beam of light, spoke’, from Latin radius ‘ray, spoke, rod’; the word later names energy streams, a figurative small amount, and a flat fish.",null,"radius",null,"Etymonline, ray (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rayon)."),contexts:[C("ray.s1","天氣","A narrow ray of sunlight entered through the gap in the curtains and fell across the desk.","一道狹窄的陽光穿過窗簾縫隙，落在桌面上。","A ray is a narrow line or beam of light.","Ray is the subject; of sunlight identifies the light source, and through marks its path.","The beam is narrow and travels through the curtain gap."),C("ray.s2","物理","The detector was shielded because a stream of X-rays can damage living tissue.","由於 X 射線可能傷害活體組織，偵測器採取了屏蔽措施。","A ray can be a stream of energy such as heat or X-rays.","Ray is the head of a stream-of-X-rays phrase; because gives the reason for shielding.","The context uses the energy-stream sense, not a visible light beam."),C("ray.s3","比喻","The first clear message from the rescue team gave the family a ray of hope.","救援隊傳來的第一則明確訊息，為家人帶來一線希望。","A ray can figuratively mean a very small amount of something good.","Ray of hope is a figurative noun phrase; gave identifies its effect.","A little good news offers a small measure of hope."),C("ray.s4","海洋生物","A spotted ray glided over the sandy seabed, its broad flat body moving like wings.","一條有斑點的鰩魚滑過沙質海床，寬扁的身體像翅膀般擺動。","A ray is also a wide, flat sea fish.","Ray is the subject; its broad flat body provides a defining feature.","The animal is the fish called a ray, not a beam of light.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The aquarium sign called a beam of sunlight swimming over the sand a ray, describing its fins and gills.","The aquarium sign called the wide, flat swimming fish a ray, describing its fins and gills.","The fish sense of ray names an animal; a beam of light cannot have fins or gills.")],quiz:[Q("ray.q1","ray.s1","meaning","A ray of light is ___.",["a narrow line or beam of light","a wide flat fish","a unit of cooked food"],"a narrow line or beam of light","The first sense names a thin beam of light.","meaning"),Q("ray.q2","ray.s2","context","An X-ray machine emits a ____ of energy through the body.",["ray","rationale","ration"],"ray","X-rays are streams of energy in this sense.","context"),Q("ray.q3","ray.s3","meaning","“A ray of hope” means ___.",["a small amount of hope","a fish in a beam","a completely certain outcome"],"a small amount of hope","Ray is figurative for a little of something positive.","meaning"),Q("ray.q4","ray.s4","context","Which animal is a ray?",["A broad, flat fish gliding over the seabed","A black bird croaking in a tree","A snake shaking its tail"],"A broad, flat fish gliding over the seabed","The fish sense refers to a wide, flat sea animal.","context")]});
D("rayon",{etymology:E("Coined in 1924 for the manufactured cellulose fiber, probably from French rayon ‘ray, beam of light’, itself from rai; the name alluded to its sheen.",null,"rai","-on","Etymonline, rayon (https://www.etymonline.com/word/rayon)."),contexts:[C("rayon.s1","紡織","The summer blouse was made of rayon, a smooth manufactured fiber derived from plant cellulose rather than silkworm silk.","這件夏季女襯衫以人造絲製成，這種光滑人造纖維來自植物纖維素，而非蠶絲。","Rayon is a manufactured textile fiber made from plant cellulose.","Rayon is the material after made of; the appositive explains its source.","Cellulose-based rayon is manufactured, unlike natural silk from silkworms.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The label described the shirt's rayon as natural silk spun by silkworms.","The label described the shirt's rayon as manufactured fiber made from plant cellulose.","Rayon is a manufactured cellulose fiber; natural silkworm silk is a different textile.")],quiz:[Q("rayon.q1","rayon.s1","meaning","Rayon is a manufactured fiber made from ___.",["plant cellulose","silkworm cocoons only","untanned cow skin"],"plant cellulose","The source sense identifies cellulose as the raw material.","meaning"),Q("rayon.q2","rayon.s1","context","Which garment is made of rayon?",["A blouse labeled as cellulose-based manufactured textile fiber","A rawhide belt","A shirt made only from silkworm silk"],"A blouse labeled as cellulose-based manufactured textile fiber","Rayon is an artificial textile fiber from plant cellulose.","context"),Q("rayon.q3","rayon.s1","confusable","Rayon and silk differ because rayon is ___.",["manufactured from cellulose, while silk comes from silkworms","an animal skin while silk is a bird","a beam of light while silk is a fish"],"manufactured from cellulose, while silk comes from silkworms","The fiber sources distinguish the materials.","confusable"),Q("rayon.q4","rayon.s1","word-choice","The fabric maker blended cotton with ____ for a smooth, draping textile.",["rayon","raven","ravine"],"rayon","Rayon is a manufactured textile fiber used in fabric blends.","word-choice")]});
D("raze",{etymology:E("An alteration of earlier rasen ‘pull or knock down’, from Old French raser ‘scrape, shave’, Medieval Latin rasare, frequentative of Latin radere ‘scrape, shave’; extended to complete demolition.",null,"radere",null,"Etymonline, raze (https://www.etymonline.com/word/raze)."),contexts:[C("raze.s1","城市規劃","The city voted to raze the unsafe warehouse and clear the site before rebuilding the block.","市政府投票決定拆平不安全的倉庫，清理基地後再重建街區。","To raze a building is to knock it down completely to the ground.","Voted to raze uses an infinitive after voted; and links demolition with site clearance.","The warehouse is to be completely demolished, not merely repaired."),C("raze.s2","比喻","The reformers hoped to raze the old system of hereditary privilege and replace it with equal rules.","改革者希望徹底廢除世襲特權的舊制度，改以平等規則取代。","Figuratively, to raze is to destroy or abolish an idea or system completely.","Raze takes system as its object; and replace states what follows its removal.","The target is an institution, not a physical building.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The council voted to raise the abandoned building to the ground, removing it completely.","The council voted to raze the abandoned building to the ground, removing it completely.","Raze means demolish; raise means lift or increase. The phrase to the ground requires raze.")],quiz:[Q("raze.q1","raze.s1","meaning","To raze a building is to ___.",["demolish it completely","paint it carefully","move into it"],"demolish it completely","Raze means knock a building flat.","meaning"),Q("raze.q2","raze.s2","context","Which use is figurative?",["They aimed to raze the corrupt system and create new rules.","They razed the brick shed with a bulldozer.","They measured the wall."],"They aimed to raze the corrupt system and create new rules.","A system is destroyed metaphorically rather than physically.","context"),Q("raze.q3","raze.s1","confusable","Choose the verb meaning “demolish”: “Workers will ____ the unsafe tower.”",["raze","raise","rays"],"raze","Raze means demolish; raise means lift or increase.","confusable"),Q("raze.q4","raze.s1","collocation","The contractor will ____ the derelict house to the ground.",["raze","reach","react"],"raze","Raze to the ground is the standard demolition phrase.","collocation")]});
D("razor",{etymology:E("From Old French rasor, raseor, from raser ‘scrape, shave’, from Medieval Latin rasare, frequentative of Latin radere ‘scrape, shave’.",null,"radere","-or","Etymonline, razor (https://www.etymonline.com/word/razor)."),contexts:[C("razor.s1","個人護理","He rinsed the safety razor after each stroke so that clipped hair would not clog its fine blade.","他每刮一下就沖洗安全剃刀，避免剪下的毛髮堵住細薄刀片。","A razor is a tool with a fine blade used to shave hair.","Razor is the object of rinsed; after each stroke marks repetition, and so that gives the purpose.","The fine blade removes hair and needs rinsing between strokes.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","She used a blunt wooden spoon as a razor to shave the hair from her face.","She used a sharp razor to shave the hair from her face.","A razor is a fine-bladed shaving tool; a wooden spoon cannot perform that function.")],quiz:[Q("razor.q1","razor.s1","meaning","A razor is a tool used to ___.",["shave hair with a fine blade","measure a light beam","make a deep valley"],"shave hair with a fine blade","The source sense describes a fine-bladed shaving tool.","meaning"),Q("razor.q2","razor.s1","context","Which object is a razor?",["A safety tool with a sharp blade for shaving","A cotton plant before processing","A snake with a tail rattle"],"A safety tool with a sharp blade for shaving","The fine blade is used to remove hair.","context"),Q("razor.q3","razor.s1","collocation","He replaced the dull ____ before shaving.",["razor","ravine","reactant"],"razor","Replace a razor is natural in the shaving context.","collocation"),Q("razor.q4","razor.s1","word-choice","The barber cleaned the ____ after trimming the client's beard.",["razor","rationale","rayon"],"razor","The barber uses a blade tool for shaving hair.","word-choice")]});
D("rd",{etymology:E("The ordinal suffix -rd is an abbreviation of third, used after numerals ending in 3 (except 13); third descends from Old English þridda and Proto-Germanic *thridja-.",null,"*thridja-","-rd","Etymonline, third (https://www.etymonline.com/word/third)."),contexts:[C("rd.s1","日期","The invitation says the lecture is on the 23rd, with rd marking the ordinal third in the written date.","邀請函寫著講座在 23 日舉行，其中 rd 是書寫序數 third 的字尾。","Rd is the letters used after suitable numerals as the short form of third.","23rd combines the numeral with the ordinal ending; the with-phrase explains the abbreviation.","The suffix marks an ordinal date, not a cardinal number.")],mistakes:[M("spelling","The editor wrote 23th in the date, using th after a number ending in 3 other than 13.","The editor wrote 23rd in the date, using rd after a number ending in 3 other than 13.","The ordinal suffix is rd for 23; th is used for 13th and most other ordinals.")],quiz:[Q("rd.q1","rd.s1","meaning","In 23rd, the letters rd abbreviate ___.",["third","thirteen","road"],"third","Rd marks the ordinal third after a suitable numeral.","meaning"),Q("rd.q2","rd.s1","context","Which is the standard ordinal form for the date after 22?",["23rd","23th","23st"],"23rd","Numbers ending in 3 take rd, except 13.","context"),Q("rd.q3","rd.s1","spelling","Choose the correct spelling.",["31st","31rd","31th"],"31st","An ordinal ending in 1 uses st, with the exception of 11.","spelling"),Q("rd.q4","rd.s1","meaning","What does the suffix in 43rd tell you?",["the number is an ordinal, meaning forty-third","the number is a fraction","the number is a road name"],"the number is an ordinal, meaning forty-third","The ending signals the order position third.","meaning")]});
D("reabsorb",{etymology:E("Formed from re- ‘back, again’ + absorb; absorb came through Old French from Latin absorbere ‘swallow up, take in’, from ab- ‘away’ + sorbere ‘suck in’.","re-","sorbere","re- + absorb","Etymonline, reabsorb (https://www.etymonline.com/word/reabsorb)."),contexts:[C("reabsorb.s1","生物學","After the filtered water returned to the kidney tubule, the body reabsorbed sodium and useful nutrients into the blood.","過濾液回到腎小管後，身體將鈉和有用養分重新吸收到血液中。","To reabsorb is to take a substance back in after it has been released or separated.","Reabsorbed takes sodium and nutrients as its objects; after and into show the sequence and destination.","The substances first leave the blood during filtration and are taken back in afterward.")],mistakes:[M("word-formation","The plant reabsorbed no water; it absorbed the water for the first time from the soil.","The plant absorbed water from the soil for the first time.","Re- means again or back; initial uptake is absorb, not reabsorb.")],quiz:[Q("reabsorb.q1","reabsorb.s1","meaning","To reabsorb a substance is to ___.",["take it back in after it was released","release it for the first time","turn it into a new element"],"take it back in after it was released","Re- marks taking in again or back.","meaning"),Q("reabsorb.q2","reabsorb.s1","context","Kidney tubules reabsorb water when they ___.",["take filtered water back into the blood","send all water out of the body","convert water into protein"],"take filtered water back into the blood","This is the return uptake after filtration.","context"),Q("reabsorb.q3","reabsorb.s1","word-formation","Which part of reabsorb means “again/back”?",["re-","ab-","-orb"],"re-","The prefix re- gives the repeated or return meaning.","word-formation"),Q("reabsorb.q4","reabsorb.s1","word-choice","After releasing a chemical, the sponge can ____ some of it from the liquid.",["reabsorb","raze","rattle"],"reabsorb","The sponge takes back in a substance already released.","word-choice")]});
D("reach",{etymology:E("From Old English ræcan, reccan ‘stretch out, extend, succeed in touching’; probably from Proto-Germanic *raikijanan, from PIE *reig- ‘stretch’. The noun later names extent or scope.",null,"*raikijanan",null,"Etymonline, reach (https://www.etymonline.com/word/reach)."),contexts:[C("reach.s1","旅遊","We reached the mountain village just before the last bus left for the coast.","我們在開往海岸的末班公車離開前，抵達了山村。","To reach a place is to arrive there.","Reached takes the destination as its object; just before sets the arrival time.","The group arrives at the village before the bus departs."),C("reach.s2","日常生活","She reached across the counter to take the receipt the clerk had set aside.","她隔著櫃檯伸手拿取店員放在一旁的收據。","To reach for or reach something is to stretch an arm to touch or take it.","Reached takes across the counter as a path; to take states the purpose.","Her arm extends toward the receipt to retrieve it."),C("reach.s3","談判","The two companies reached an agreement after three days of talks.","兩家公司經過三天會談後達成協議。","To reach can mean to get to a particular level, agreement, or number.","Reached takes agreement as its object; after gives the process duration.","The parties arrive at a settled agreement."),C("reach.s4","通訊","I tried to reach the clinic by phone, but the line stayed busy all morning.","我試著打電話聯絡診所，但整個上午電話線都占線。","To reach someone is to succeed in speaking or communicating with them.","Reach takes the clinic as its object; by phone gives the method, but signals the attempt failed.","The caller did not succeed in making contact."),C("reach.s5","能力","The top shelf is beyond my reach unless I use the step stool.","除非使用踏腳凳，否則最上層架子超出我伸手可及的範圍。","Reach as a noun is the distance one can extend or one's scope or power.","Beyond my reach is a noun phrase after is; unless introduces the needed condition.","Without the stool, the shelf lies outside the distance the speaker can touch.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","We reached to the station at noon after a short train ride.","We reached the station at noon after a short train ride.","When reach means arrive at a destination, it takes a direct object without to.")],quiz:[Q("reach.q1","reach.s1","meaning","If a traveler reaches the airport, the traveler ___.",["arrives there","stretches an arm toward it only","sets a food limit"],"arrives there","This is the destination sense of reach.","meaning"),Q("reach.q2","reach.s2","context","Which action means physically reach for an object?",["Stretch across a desk to pick up a pen","Arrive at a station","Agree on a contract"],"Stretch across a desk to pick up a pen","The arm extends to touch or take the object.","context"),Q("reach.q3","reach.s3","collocation","After negotiation, the sides finally ____ an agreement.",["reached","reacted","reabsorbed"],"reached","Reach an agreement means arrive at a settled agreement.","collocation"),Q("reach.q4","reach.s4","grammar","Choose the correct sentence for successful phone contact.",["I reached the nurse by phone.","I reached to the nurse by phone.","I reached at the nurse by phone."],"I reached the nurse by phone.","Reach meaning contact takes a direct object without a preposition.","grammar")]});
D("reachable",{etymology:E("Formed from reach + -able, the suffix from Old French -able and Latin -abilis ‘capable of being’; the adjective means able to be reached or obtained.",null,"reach","-able","Etymonline, readable (https://www.etymonline.com/word/readability) (formation pattern -able; reach in https://www.etymonline.com/word/reach)."),contexts:[C("reachable.s1","交通","The cabin is reachable by a marked trail from the north road, even after the bridge closes to cars.","即使橋梁禁止車輛通行，仍可從北側道路沿標示步道抵達小屋。","Reachable means able to be reached or obtained.","Reachable modifies cabin; by a marked trail gives the access route, and even after adds a constraint.","The route allows people to get to the cabin despite the road closure.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The island was reachable only by foot, although it lay 200 miles offshore with no bridge or boat service.","The island was unreachable by foot because it lay 200 miles offshore with no bridge or boat service.","The stated distance and lack of transport make the island not reachable by foot.")],quiz:[Q("reachable.q1","reachable.s1","meaning","If a place is reachable, it is ___.",["possible to get to","already destroyed","unprocessed"],"possible to get to","Reachable means able to be reached.","meaning"),Q("reachable.q2","reachable.s1","context","Which route makes a cabin reachable?",["A public trail leads directly to it.","A map shows no path and the area is closed.","The cabin exists only in a drawing."],"A public trail leads directly to it.","A usable trail provides access.","context"),Q("reachable.q3","reachable.s1","word-formation","Reachable means ___.",["able to be reached","reaching again","a place that cannot be reached"],"able to be reached","The suffix -able means capable of being reached.","word-formation"),Q("reachable.q4","reachable.s1","word-choice","The help desk is ____ by phone until 8 p.m.",["reachable","ravenous","raw"],"reachable","The desk staff can be contacted by phone.","word-choice")]});
D("react",{etymology:E("From re- ‘back’ + act, formed in the 1640s for an opposite action; later it also meant respond to events, undergo chemical change, or oppose a reform.","re-","agere","re- + act","Etymonline, react (https://www.etymonline.com/word/react)."),contexts:[C("react.s1","人際","When the alarm sounded, the staff reacted calmly and guided visitors toward the marked exits.","警報響起時，工作人員冷靜應對，引導訪客前往標示出口。","To react is to behave in a particular way because something has happened.","Reacted is followed by manner adverb calmly; and links response and action.","The alarm event caused the staff's calm behavior."),C("react.s2","化學","Iron reacts with oxygen and moisture to form rust on an unprotected surface.","鐵會與氧氣和水分起反應，在未受保護的表面形成鏽蝕。","To react chemically is to change when mixed or brought into contact with another substance.","Reacts with names the other substances; to form gives the result.","Iron changes through a chemical process with oxygen and moisture."),C("react.s3","政治","Some residents reacted against the proposed restriction by organizing a petition in favor of the earlier rules.","部分居民反對新提議的限制，發起請願支持原有規則。","To react against a change can mean oppose it by moving in the opposite direction.","Reacted against takes the restriction as its target; by introduces the method of opposition.","The petition resists the proposed change and supports the previous policy.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The iron reacted with oxygen to form rust, so it merely changed its facial expression at the chemical level.","The iron reacted chemically with oxygen to form rust.","React in chemistry means undergo a substance-changing process, not display an emotional response.")],quiz:[Q("react.q1","react.s1","meaning","When people react to news, they ___.",["respond or behave because of it","become a starting chemical","arrive at a place"],"respond or behave because of it","This is the general response sense.","meaning"),Q("react.q2","react.s2","context","Which sentence uses react in chemistry?",["Acid reacts with the metal and produces a gas.","The audience reacted with applause.","The committee reacted against the rule."],"Acid reacts with the metal and produces a gas.","The substances undergo a chemical change and form a product.","context"),Q("react.q3","react.s3","context","Residents react against a new rule when they ___.",["organize to oppose the change","quietly implement it","measure its temperature"],"organize to oppose the change","The sense is to oppose a development by moving against it.","context"),Q("react.q4","react.s1","grammar","Choose the correct pattern: “How did the patient ____ to the medicine?”",["react","reach to","reacted"],"react","After did, the verb takes its base form; react to is the usual construction.","grammar")]});
D("reactant",{etymology:E("Formed from react + -ant, the agent or participant suffix from Latin -antem; in chemistry a reactant is a starting substance consumed as products form.",null,"agere","-ant","Etymonline, react (https://www.etymonline.com/word/react) and -ant (https://www.etymonline.com/word/-ant)."),contexts:[C("reactant.s1","化學","In the equation, hydrogen and oxygen are the reactants on the left; water is the product on the right.","在此反應式中，氫和氧是左側的反應物，水則是右側的生成物。","A reactant is a starting chemical that is consumed as products form.","Reactants is linked to the left side of the equation; the semicolon contrasts them with the product.","Hydrogen and oxygen are present at the start and are used to form water.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The lab report called the water formed at the end of the reaction a reactant and the starting hydrogen a product.","The lab report called the starting hydrogen a reactant and the water formed at the end a product.","Reactants are starting substances consumed during a reaction; products are formed by it.")],quiz:[Q("reactant.q1","reactant.s1","meaning","A reactant is a substance that ___.",["is present at the start and is used up as products form","is always the final product","cannot take part in a reaction"],"is present at the start and is used up as products form","That is the chemistry definition of reactant.","meaning"),Q("reactant.q2","reactant.s1","context","In 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, hydrogen and oxygen are the ___.",["reactants","products","catalysts only"],"reactants","They are the starting materials consumed to form water.","context"),Q("reactant.q3","reactant.s1","confusable","Which statement distinguishes reactant from product?",["A reactant starts the process; a product is formed by it.","A reactant is always a vessel.","The terms are interchangeable in equations."],"A reactant starts the process; a product is formed by it.","The source definition identifies reactants as starting chemicals.","confusable"),Q("reactant.q4","reactant.s1","word-choice","The chemist measured each ____ before beginning the reaction.",["reactant","ravine","rationale"],"reactant","The starting chemicals are measured before they react.","word-choice")]});
D("reaction",{etymology:E("From re- ‘back, again’ + action, modeled on French réaction and Medieval Latin reactionem from reagere ‘react’, re- + agere ‘do, perform’; chemistry use is recorded by 1836.","re-","agere","-tion","Etymonline, reaction (https://www.etymonline.com/word/reaction)."),contexts:[C("reaction.s1","社交","Her reaction to the news was a long pause followed by a question about the family's safety.","她聽到消息後先沉默許久，接著詢問家人的安全。","A reaction is a response to something that happens.","Reaction is the subject complement; to the news identifies its trigger, and followed by sequences the response.","The pause and question are her response to the news."),C("reaction.s2","化學","The reaction between vinegar and baking soda released bubbles of carbon dioxide.","醋與小蘇打之間的化學反應釋出二氧化碳氣泡。","A chemical reaction is a process in which substances change into other substances.","Reaction is followed by between to name the substances; released states the result.","The starting substances change and produce carbon dioxide gas.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The bubbles produced when vinegar and baking soda change into new substances are a reaction, but the new process is called their reactants.","The bubbles are evidence of a reaction; vinegar and baking soda are the reactants.","Reaction names the process; reactants are starting chemicals, not the process itself.")],quiz:[Q("reaction.q1","reaction.s1","meaning","A person's reaction to a surprise is ___.",["their response to it","the starting chemical","the result of a vote"],"their response to it","The general sense means a response to an event.","meaning"),Q("reaction.q2","reaction.s2","context","Which is a chemical reaction?",["Two substances change and produce a gas.","A person smiles at a joke.","A train arrives at a station."],"Two substances change and produce a gas.","Substances changing into new substances is a chemical reaction.","context"),Q("reaction.q3","reaction.s2","confusable","In a chemical equation, reaction names the ___, while reactant names a starting substance.",["process of change","finished container","measurement of the vessel"],"process of change","Reaction is the process; reactants are the materials that undergo it.","confusable"),Q("reaction.q4","reaction.s1","collocation","The manager asked for everyone's ____ to the proposed schedule.",["reaction","reactant","raven"],"reaction","Reaction to is the standard phrase for responses to a proposal.","collocation")]});
D("reactive",{etymology:E("Formed from react + -ive, an adjective suffix from Latin -ivus; it can describe chemical susceptibility or a person or system that responds quickly to events.",null,"agere","-ive","Etymonline, reactive (https://www.etymonline.com/word/reactive)."),contexts:[C("reactive.s1","化學","The technician stored the reactive powder away from moisture because contact with water could release heat.","技術員將這種具反應性的粉末遠離潮氣保存，因為接觸水可能釋放熱量。","Reactive means able to react chemically with other substances.","Reactive modifies powder; because gives the reason for special storage.","The powder can undergo a chemical change when exposed to water."),C("reactive.s2","人際","The manager was reactive to every complaint, changing the plan immediately before checking whether the reports were accurate.","經理對每項投訴都立刻起反應，尚未核實報告是否正確就更改計畫。","Reactive can describe someone quick to respond to people or events.","Reactive is followed by to complaints; changing explains the quick response.","The manager responds promptly, perhaps without first investigating.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The sealed inert gas was highly reactive with every substance, yet it never changed or formed a compound in any trial.","The sealed inert gas was unreactive under the tested conditions because it did not change or form a compound.","Reactive describes a substance able to undergo chemical reactions; the evidence shows no reaction.")],quiz:[Q("reactive.q1","reactive.s1","meaning","A reactive chemical is one that ___.",["can undergo chemical change with other substances","cannot interact under any conditions","has already reached an agreement"],"can undergo chemical change with other substances","This is the chemical sense of reactive.","meaning"),Q("reactive.q2","reactive.s2","context","A reactive supervisor changes a policy every time one person complains. The adjective describes someone who ___.",["responds quickly to events or people","is a chemical starting material","never responds at all"],"responds quickly to events or people","Reactive can refer to a quick response to people or events.","context"),Q("reactive.q3","reactive.s1","word-formation","Reactive is formed from which base verb?",["react","read","reach"],"react","The adjective is react + -ive.","word-formation"),Q("reactive.q4","reactive.s2","confusable","A proactive planner anticipates problems; a reactive planner usually ___.",["responds after a problem or event occurs","acts before any event is possible","measures chemical quantities only"],"responds after a problem or event occurs","Reactive emphasizes response to events, unlike proactive anticipation.","confusable")]});
D("reactor",{etymology:E("A Latin-style agent noun from react + -or; Etymonline records reactor in 1835 for ‘one that reacts’, with later electrical and nuclear-engineering senses.",null,"agere","-or","Etymonline, reactor (https://www.etymonline.com/word/reactor)."),contexts:[C("reactor.s1","核能","Engineers monitored the reactor's temperature and control rods to keep the nuclear reaction contained and steady.","工程師監測反應堆的溫度與控制棒，使核反應維持在受控且穩定的狀態。","A reactor is a vessel or installation designed to contain and control a reaction.","Reactor is the object of monitored; to keep gives the purpose of monitoring.","The installation contains the reaction and engineers regulate its conditions.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The laboratory called the hydrogen consumed at the beginning of an experiment the reactor.","The laboratory called the vessel that contains and controls the reaction the reactor.","A reactant is a starting chemical; a reactor is the apparatus or installation containing the process.")],quiz:[Q("reactor.q1","reactor.s1","meaning","A chemical or nuclear reactor is designed to ___.",["contain and control a reaction","serve as the starting chemical","measure a person's response"],"contain and control a reaction","The source sense is a vessel or installation for controlling a reaction.","meaning"),Q("reactor.q2","reactor.s1","context","Which item is a reactor?",["A vessel where a controlled reaction occurs","A bottle of starting reactant","A report describing a result"],"A vessel where a controlled reaction occurs","The vessel contains and controls the process.","context"),Q("reactor.q3","reactor.s1","confusable","A reactor differs from a reactant because the reactor is ___.",["the equipment or installation; the reactant is a starting chemical","always the chemical product","a person who reads aloud"],"the equipment or installation; the reactant is a starting chemical","The apparatus and starting substance have different roles.","confusable"),Q("reactor.q4","reactor.s1","word-choice","Operators checked the pressure gauges around the industrial ____.",["reactor","ravenous","ravine"],"reactor","Pressure gauges monitor the vessel containing a controlled process.","word-choice")]});
D("read",{etymology:E("From Old English rædan, gerædan ‘advise, counsel, interpret; read’, from Proto-Germanic *redan and PIE *re- ‘reason, count’; the older sense linked reading with interpreting signs.",null,"*redan",null,"Etymonline, read (https://www.etymonline.com/word/read)."),contexts:[C("read.s1","教育","The child read the short poem aloud twice, then explained what each stanza meant.","孩子將短詩朗讀兩遍，接著說明每節的意思。","To read is to look at written words and understand them, or to say them aloud.","Read takes the poem as its object; aloud specifies speaking, and then sequences explanation.","The child both vocalizes the text and understands it."),C("read.s2","人際","I could read her disappointment from the way she lowered her eyes and stopped asking questions.","從她垂下目光、不再提問的樣子，我看得出她很失望。","To read can mean understand signs, a mood, or a hidden meaning.","Read takes disappointment as its object; from introduces the behavioral evidence.","The speaker interprets nonverbal signs to infer her mood."),C("read.s3","儀器","The thermometer reads 18 degrees, although the room feels warmer near the sunny window.","溫度計顯示十八度，儘管靠近向陽窗戶的地方感覺較暖。","A display or text can read a figure or statement by showing or stating it.","Reads takes 18 degrees as its complement; although introduces a contrast in perception.","The instrument displays a measured value."),C("read.s4","書評","The novel is a quick read for commuters, with short chapters and a clear plot.","這本小說適合通勤時快速閱讀，章節短、情節清楚。","Read as a noun can mean something that is good or bad to read, or an act of reading.","A quick read is a noun phrase; for commuters names the audience.","The book is characterized as easy and quick to read.")],mistakes:[M("verb-form","Yesterday she read the entire report aloud, and then she reads the key paragraph again for the team.","Yesterday she read the entire report aloud, and then she read the key paragraph again for the team.","In past narration, both completed actions use the past form read; its spelling matches the present form but pronunciation differs.")],quiz:[Q("read.q1","read.s1","meaning","To read a page aloud means to ___.",["say its written words so others can hear","guess a person's mood","show a temperature"],"say its written words so others can hear","This is the spoken-text sense of read.","meaning"),Q("read.q2","read.s2","context","“I read his expression as worry” means I ___.",["interpreted his expression and understood his mood","spoke the expression aloud","measured it in degrees"],"interpreted his expression and understood his mood","Read here means interpret a sign or mood.","context"),Q("read.q3","read.s3","meaning","If a meter reads 18, it ___.",["shows the figure 18","understands a person's feelings","is a book to read"],"shows the figure 18","This sense means display a figure or statement.","meaning"),Q("read.q4","read.s4","context","A “light read” is usually ___.",["something easy or enjoyable to read","a tool for measuring light","a book that cannot be opened"],"something easy or enjoyable to read","Read as a noun can describe a reading experience or text.","context")]});
D("read out",{etymology:E("A phrasal verb combining read, from Old English rædan ‘interpret/read’, with out, which can mark completion or making words public; read out means read aloud to listeners.",null,"*redan","out + read","Etymonline, read (https://www.etymonline.com/word/read); out (https://www.etymonline.com/word/out)."),contexts:[C("read out.s1","會議","The secretary read out the revised safety instructions so that every person in the room could hear them.","秘書宣讀修訂後的安全指示，讓房間裡每個人都能聽見。","To read something out is to read it aloud to an audience.","Read out takes instructions as its object; so that introduces the purpose.","The secretary vocalizes the written instructions for everyone present.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The secretary read out the notice silently to herself, and no one in the room could hear it.","The secretary read the notice silently to herself, without reading it out to the room.","Read out means read aloud to listeners; silent reading does not fit this phrasal verb.")],quiz:[Q("read out.q1","read out.s1","meaning","To read out a message is to ___.",["say it aloud for people to hear","read it silently without an audience","write it from memory"],"say it aloud for people to hear","The phrasal verb means read aloud to an audience.","meaning"),Q("read out.q2","read out.s1","context","Which action is reading out?",["A chairperson speaks the written motion aloud to the meeting.","A student scans a page silently alone.","A clerk files a blank form."],"A chairperson speaks the written motion aloud to the meeting.","The written motion is vocalized for listeners.","context"),Q("read out.q3","read out.s1","grammar","Choose the correct sentence.",["The host read out the names.","The host read out the names silently to herself.","The host readed out the names."],"The host read out the names.","Read out is the correct phrasal verb and implies reading aloud; read is irregular.","grammar"),Q("read out.q4","read out.s1","collocation","At the ceremony, the announcer will ____ the award winner's name.",["read out","reabsorb","raze"],"read out","The announcer reads the name aloud for the audience.","collocation")]});
D("readability",{etymology:E("Formed from readable + -ity: readable combines read + -able, and -ity makes an abstract noun for a quality or condition; the word was recorded in 1829.",null,"read","-ability","Etymonline, readability (https://www.etymonline.com/word/readability)."),contexts:[C("readability.s1","出版","The editor improved the manual's readability by shortening long sentences, defining jargon, and adding headings.","編輯透過縮短長句、解釋術語並加入標題，提升了手冊的易讀性。","Readability is the quality that makes writing clear through wording, layout, and sentence length.","Readability is the object of improved; by lists methods, and and links the changes.","Clear wording, manageable sentences, and headings make the manual easier to read.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The report's readability was poor because every paragraph used plain language, short sentences, and clear headings.","The report's readability was high because it used plain language, short sentences, and clear headings.","These features generally improve readability rather than make a text difficult to read.")],quiz:[Q("readability.q1","readability.s1","meaning","Readability describes how ___.",["easy and clear writing is to read","fast a person can run","much water a person receives"],"easy and clear writing is to read","Readability is the quality that makes writing clear and accessible.","meaning"),Q("readability.q2","readability.s1","context","Which edit is most likely to improve a document's readability?",["Define technical terms and break up long sentences","Remove all headings and punctuation","Replace familiar words with unexplained jargon"],"Define technical terms and break up long sentences","These edits make wording and structure easier to follow.","context"),Q("readability.q3","readability.s1","word-formation","Readability is built from readable plus the abstract noun suffix ___.",["-ity","-less","-ous"],"-ity","The suffix -ity forms a noun naming a quality or condition.","word-formation"),Q("readability.q4","readability.s1","word-choice","Large type and clear headings can increase the ____ of an instruction sheet.",["readability","reactant","ravine"],"readability","The features make the sheet easier to read.","word-choice")]});
})();
